    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d59">

                <pb facs="0092" n="38" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg38"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/9–644</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Deputy Director of the Office of European
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Matthews</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Ambassador in Canada</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-09-06">September 6, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Ray</hi>: As you know, I pointed out to Admiral
                    Leahy the importance we attach, with a view to your position in Canada, to your
                    presence for at least a part of the forthcoming talks at Quebec. The Admiral
                    fully understood and telephoned me this afternoon to say that he had discussed
                    the matter with the President, and that the President <pb facs="0093" n="39"
                        xml:id="pg39"/> wishes you to come to see him at Quebec on the 11th or 12th
                    of September. When you arrive, I suggest that you get in touch again with
                    Admiral Leahy.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Hastily,</p>
                <p>As ever,</p>
                <closer><signed>H F[<hi rendition="#small-caps">reeman</hi>] M[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">atthews</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
